# GameMatch — environment for the compose stack.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored (.env.* with !.env.example); this file is the committed
# template. Two complete configurations follow, and one docker-compose.yml
# serves both. To deploy to a VPS: comment out every line of the local block,
# then uncomment every line of the VPS block except DEV_OTP, which must stay
# commented. Each block is a complete set of settings — nothing has to be
# carried across from the other, and nothing has to be looked up anywhere else.
# The prose is kept outside the blocks on purpose, so uncommenting a block
# cannot uncomment an explanation.
#
# The block markers bound those instructions for a reader and nothing more.
# This file is not machine-readable: a script that strips every leading "#"
# from the VPS marker to the end of file trips on the markers themselves and
# docker compose rejects the result. That failure is loud, which is fine.
#
# WEB PUSH at the end is optional and applies to either host.

# APP_DEBUG=true below makes every one-time code the constant DEV_OTP, and
# returns it in the /v1/auth/otp/start response as devCode, so anyone who can
# reach this site can sign in as any phone number. It is safe for a browser on
# your own machine and nowhere else. GAMEMATCH_SITE=localhost serves HTTPS with
# Caddy's internal CA, which no phone trusts.
# --- local: this machine (APP_ENV=local) -----------------------------------
GAMEMATCH_SITE=localhost
HTTP_PORT=80
HTTPS_PORT=443
APP_ENV=local
APP_DEBUG=true
DEV_OTP=123456
HOUSE_USER_ID=00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

# Read this before editing the block below.
#
# Set APP_ENV=production FIRST. That one line is the entire guardrail:
# Config.Validate() is almost inert outside production (it still rejects an
# unknown APP_ENV), and APP_ENV falls back
# to "local" when it is absent. A VPS configured with a real domain but without
# it starts happily and serves a real Let's Encrypt certificate, and then every
# sign-in fails silently: codes are generated and thrown away instead of being
# sent, so nobody ever receives one. With APP_ENV set, the server refuses to
# boot and names each missing variable, so the rest can be filled in at your
# own pace.
#
# Replace the GAMEMATCH_SITE placeholder with your own domain. Left as it is,
# Caddy issues for gamematch.example.com and every visitor gets a name mismatch.
#
# Once APP_ENV=production is in effect, seven of these are refused at boot.
# APP_DEBUG=true, because it makes every code the constant DEV_OTP and returns
# it in the response as devCode, so anyone who can reach the site signs in as
# any phone number. DEV_OTP on its own does nothing while APP_DEBUG is false --
# the random code wins -- and is refused as the second lever, which goes live
# the moment APP_DEBUG is set.
# SMS_PROVIDER=log, because it never delivers: the log provider discards
# message bodies on purpose and keeps only a masked number, so without Twilio
# no code ever reaches a phone and sign-in cannot complete. The three Twilio
# values must each be non-empty for that same reason. TURNSTILE_SECRET is the
# exception: with it unset the verifier accepts every token, so an IP working
# through OTP failures is never challenged.
#
# DEV_OTP is the one line in this block that stays commented. Uncommenting it
# by accident is harmless — an empty value is read as unset — but it is never
# what you want here.
#
# Apple and Google sign-in cannot be configured. The server answers those
# routes with "Sign-in is not configured yet. Use a phone code.", so there are
# no keys for them to set here.
# --- VPS: public host (APP_ENV=production) ----------------------------------
#APP_ENV=production
#GAMEMATCH_SITE=gamematch.example.com
#HTTP_PORT=80
#HTTPS_PORT=443
#APP_DEBUG=false
#DEV_OTP=
#SMS_PROVIDER=twilio
#TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
#TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
#TWILIO_FROM=
#TURNSTILE_SECRET=
#HOUSE_USER_ID=00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

# Generate a keypair with: gamematch vapid
# --- optional: web push, either host ---------------------------------------
#VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
#VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
#VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:ops@example.com
